1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,830
一只机器狗，背着七十公斤，
A robot dog carried seventy kilograms

2
00:00:02,830 --> 00:00:04,120
爬上了泰山。
up Mount Tai.

3
00:00:04,120 --> 00:00:05,850
七十公斤是什么概念？
How heavy is seventy kilograms?

4
00:00:05,850 --> 00:00:07,870
差不多背着一个成年人。
About one grown-up on its back.

5
00:00:07,870 --> 00:00:11,020
这是11月2日开赛的泰山机器人登山赛，
This was the Mount Tai robot climbing contest that opened November second,

6
00:00:11,020 --> 00:00:12,640
它拿了负重赛冠军。
and it won the load race.

7
00:00:12,640 --> 00:00:15,410
据报道，它的额定负重只有五十公斤，
Reportedly its rated load is only fifty kilograms.

8
00:00:15,410 --> 00:00:16,990
比赛这段直接超载。
On this stretch it was overloaded.

9
00:00:16,990 --> 00:00:18,500
今天的烧脑问题：
Today's brain teaser:

10
00:00:18,500 --> 00:00:22,010
机器狗背七十公斤爬泰山，到底累不累？
does a robot dog get tired hauling seventy kilos up Mount Tai?

11
00:00:22,010 --> 00:00:23,640
先认识主角：小灵，
Meet our hero, Lingling,

12
00:00:23,640 --> 00:00:25,560
一只四条腿的机器狗。
a four-legged robot dog.

13
00:00:25,560 --> 00:00:26,730
它没有肌肉，
It has no muscles.

14
00:00:26,730 --> 00:00:28,790
每条腿上是几个电机。
Each leg has a few motors.

15
00:00:28,790 --> 00:00:30,040
爬山，说白了就是
Climbing is really just

16
00:00:30,040 --> 00:00:31,420
把东西往高处搬。
lifting stuff higher.

17
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:33,440
每一级台阶，就像把箱子
Every step is like lifting a box

18
00:00:33,440 --> 00:00:34,840
搬上一层货架。
onto the next shelf.

19
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:35,990
物理课的公式：
The physics rule:

20
00:00:35,990 --> 00:00:38,390
做的功 = 重量 × 高度。
work equals weight times height.

21
00:00:38,390 --> 00:00:40,770
估算一下：七十公斤抬高一米，
Rough estimate: lifting seventy kilos one meter

22
00:00:40,770 --> 00:00:41,910
大约七百焦。
takes about seven hundred joules.

23
00:00:41,910 --> 00:00:43,580
一级台阶十几厘米，
One step is fifteen centimeters or so.

24
00:00:43,580 --> 00:00:45,360
一级就要一百多焦。
That is over one hundred joules per step.

25
00:00:45,360 --> 00:00:47,170
要是一路背到泰山顶，
If it hauled all the way to the summit,

26
00:00:47,170 --> 00:00:49,100
估算要抬高一千多米。
that is over a thousand meters up, roughly.

27
00:00:49,100 --> 00:00:50,930
七十公斤抬一千多米，
Seventy kilos up a thousand meters

28
00:00:50,930 --> 00:00:52,880
算下来将近一百万焦。
works out to nearly a million joules.

29
00:00:52,880 --> 00:00:54,270
一百万焦是多少？
How much is a million joules?

30
00:00:54,270 --> 00:00:56,470
大约四块大号充电宝的电。
About four big power banks.

31
00:00:56,470 --> 00:00:59,180
可电机会发热，腿还要找平衡，
But motors heat up and legs keep balancing,

32
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:02,390
实际耗的电得多好几倍，这是推测。
so the real bill is several times more. That's our guess.

33
00:01:02,390 --> 00:01:04,020
反转一：走快走慢，
Twist one: fast or slow,

34
00:01:04,020 --> 00:01:05,760
这份功一分都不少。
the work stays exactly the same.

35
00:01:05,760 --> 00:01:07,170
一口气冲上去，
Rush up in one go,

36
00:01:07,170 --> 00:01:09,700
和歇十次再上去，一样多。
or rest ten times, it is the same amount.

37
00:01:09,700 --> 00:01:11,890
走得快，只是每秒花得多，
Going fast only spends more per second.

38
00:01:11,890 --> 00:01:12,920
这叫功率。
That is called power.

39
00:01:12,920 --> 00:01:13,780
就像花钱：
Like paying for something:

40
00:01:13,780 --> 00:01:16,640
总价一样，只是一次付还是分期付。
same price, all at once or in installments.

41
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:18,230
那为啥是四条腿，
So why four legs

42
00:01:18,230 --> 00:01:19,530
不是两条腿？
and not two?

43
00:01:19,530 --> 00:01:20,400
想想凳子：
Think of a stool:

44
00:01:20,400 --> 00:01:22,960
三条腿的凳子，怎么放都不晃。
a three-legged stool never wobbles.

45
00:01:22,960 --> 00:01:24,570
机器狗抬一条腿，
When the robot dog lifts one leg,

46
00:01:24,570 --> 00:01:26,310
还剩三条腿撑着。
three are still holding it up.

47
00:01:26,310 --> 00:01:28,760
两条腿的人形机器人抬一条腿，
When a two-legged humanoid lifts one leg,

48
00:01:28,760 --> 00:01:31,150
只剩一个点，得一直找平衡。
only one point is left, so it must keep balancing.

49
00:01:31,150 --> 00:01:32,280
所以背重物，
So for heavy loads,

50
00:01:32,280 --> 00:01:34,090
四条腿天生占便宜。
four legs have a built-in edge.

51
00:01:34,090 --> 00:01:35,380
那人形机器人呢？
What about humanoids?

52
00:01:35,380 --> 00:01:38,240
据报道，它们也在乱台阶上比了竞速。
Reportedly they raced on the messy steps too.

53
00:01:38,240 --> 00:01:39,590
两条腿虽然难，
Two legs are harder,

54
00:01:39,590 --> 00:01:42,610
可人走的路，全是给两条腿修的。
but every path people walk was built for two legs.

55
00:01:42,610 --> 00:01:44,130
反转二，最反直觉：
Twist two, the strangest:

56
00:01:44,130 --> 00:01:45,930
站着不动，也在耗电。
standing still also burns power.

57
00:01:45,930 --> 00:01:47,170
按物理课的定义，
By the physics definition,

58
00:01:47,170 --> 00:01:49,000
举着不动，做的功是零。
holding still does zero work.

59
00:01:49,000 --> 00:01:50,720
可电机要使劲撑住，
But the motors push to hold on.

60
00:01:50,720 --> 00:01:53,310
电流一直在流，全变成了热。
Current keeps flowing, and it all turns into heat.

61
00:01:53,310 --> 00:01:55,300
你端着一桶水站着不动，
Hold a bucket of water without moving,

62
00:01:55,300 --> 00:01:56,690
胳膊照样会酸。
and your arm still gets sore.

63
00:01:56,690 --> 00:01:58,620
所以机器狗不会“累”，
So the robot dog does not get tired,

64
00:01:58,620 --> 00:02:00,680
但电机会热，电池会掉。
but its motors heat up and its battery drains.

65
00:02:00,680 --> 00:02:02,550
反转三：泰山的台阶，
Twist three: on Mount Tai,

66
00:02:02,550 --> 00:02:04,540
最难的不是高，是乱。
the hard part is not the height, it is the mess.

67
00:02:04,540 --> 00:02:07,110
据报道，台阶高低宽窄都不一样，
Reportedly the steps vary in height and width,

68
00:02:07,110 --> 00:02:08,780
每一步都得重新算。
so every step needs a new calculation.

69
00:02:08,780 --> 00:02:10,810
机器狗靠眼睛和腿上的感觉，
The dog uses cameras and the feel in its legs

70
00:02:10,810 --> 00:02:12,490
一步一步“摸”着走。
to feel its way, step by step.

71
00:02:12,490 --> 00:02:14,230
再说咱们的挑山工：
Now the human porters of Mount Tai:

72
00:02:14,230 --> 00:02:17,250
据央视报道，一趟挑三四十公斤。
according to CCTV, about thirty to forty kilos a trip.

73
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:18,780
机器狗背七十公斤，
The robot dog carried seventy,

74
00:02:18,780 --> 00:02:20,590
力气上已经赢了一倍。
about double on pure strength.

75
00:02:20,590 --> 00:02:22,410
可挑山工能挑一整天，
But porters can go all day.

76
00:02:22,410 --> 00:02:24,340
机器狗得找地方充电。
The robot dog needs to find a charger.

77
00:02:24,340 --> 00:02:27,420
据报道，登山赛上还有人穿着助力外骨骼，
Reportedly, one climber wore an assist exoskeleton

78
00:02:27,420 --> 00:02:29,490
大约一小时就上了中天门。
and reached the halfway gate in about an hour.

79
00:02:29,490 --> 00:02:31,410
机器不一定要替人爬山，
Machines don't have to climb for us.

80
00:02:31,410 --> 00:02:32,930
也可以帮人爬山。
They can help us climb.

81
00:02:32,930 --> 00:02:36,570
友情提示：七十公斤、五十公斤额定是据报道，
Fine print: seventy kilos and the fifty kilo rating are as reported.

82
00:02:36,570 --> 00:02:38,770
七百焦、一百多焦是估算。
Seven hundred joules and over one hundred per step are estimates.

83
00:02:38,770 --> 00:02:40,350
比赛是一天的成绩，
A contest is one day's result,

84
00:02:40,350 --> 00:02:42,580
离天天上山干活还有距离。
still far from hauling up the mountain every day.

85
00:02:42,580 --> 00:02:44,330
所以，机器狗累不累？
So does the robot dog get tired?

86
00:02:44,330 --> 00:02:46,900
它不会累，只会热、只会没电。
It never gets tired. It only gets hot and runs out of battery.

87
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,790
泰山不是一口气爬上去的，
Nobody climbs Mount Tai in one go.

88
00:02:48,790 --> 00:02:51,030
是一级一级“抬”上去的。
It gets lifted, one step at a time.

